WEBVTT

1
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:22.841
Jim and I went to look more closely at a hill I'd seen when I first explored the

2
00:00:22.941 --> 00:00:28.302
island. It was steep and covered with bushes, so it was a hard climb.

3
00:00:29.683 --> 00:00:33.884
Almost at the top, we found a rock cave big enough for Jim to stand up in.

4
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:41.363
Jim suggested that we put all our gear in the cave and then hide the canoe among the

5
00:00:41.423 --> 00:00:42.703
willow branches on the shore.

6
00:00:42.723 --> 00:00:50.886
"If anyone comes to the island," he said, "we can hide in the cave quickly and then no

7
00:00:51.006 --> 00:00:52.347
one will ever find us.

8
00:00:53.227 --> 00:01:00.150
Besides," he reminded me, "the little birds said it's going to rain, and the cave will keep our

9
00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:00.930
things dry."

10
00:01:02.091 --> 00:01:04.452
I thought this was a good idea, so we did it.

11
00:01:05.564 --> 00:01:09.946
Then we built a fire outside the cave and cooked a fish and cornbread dinner.

12
00:01:11.346 --> 00:01:16.989
We spread our blankets inside the cave for a carpet, and while we were eating dinner in there,

13
00:01:17.349 --> 00:01:18.849
it began to thunder and lightning.

14
00:01:20.150 --> 00:01:24.112
The wind howled and the rain poured down, just as Jim had predicted.

15
00:01:24.132 --> 00:01:27.633
"Jim, this is nice," I said.

16
00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:30.174
"I wouldn't want to be anywhere but here."

17
00:01:32.835 --> 00:01:36.837
The river kept rising for over a week and finally flooded the banks.

18
00:01:38.238 --> 00:01:42.780
The lower parts of the island were under a meter of water, and we paddled around them in

19
00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:43.280
our canoe.

20
00:01:45.121 --> 00:01:48.223
At night, when no one could see us, we went out on the river.

21
00:01:49.584 --> 00:01:54.066
One night, we caught a big lumber raft made of pine logs and hid it by the shore.

22
00:01:55.767 --> 00:01:59.789
Another night, just before dawn, we saw a whole house floating down the river.

23
00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:04.232
At daybreak, we paddled over to it and looked in the window.

24
00:02:05.640 --> 00:02:10.843
We could see some furniture, some clothes hanging, and something that looked like a man lying on the

25
00:02:10.903 --> 00:02:14.365
floor. We called to him, but he didn't move.

26
00:02:14.385 --> 00:02:17.687
"He's not asleep," Jim said.

27
00:02:17.707 --> 00:02:19.048
"He's dead.

28
00:02:19.668 --> 00:02:22.630
You stay here, and I'll climb in and have a look."

29
00:02:24.391 --> 00:02:27.993
After a minute, he called back to me to say that the man had been shot in the

30
00:02:28.033 --> 00:02:32.736
back. He pulled some rags over him to hide him, and then he let me come in.

31
00:02:34.076 --> 00:02:35.798
I didn't look at the dead man at all.

32
00:02:37.019 --> 00:02:43.445
There were men's and women's clothes in the house, and useful things like candles and candlesticks, a tin

33
00:02:43.485 --> 00:02:45.347
cup, and fishing line and hooks.

34
00:02:46.588 --> 00:02:50.932
By the time we piled everything in the canoe, the house had floated a long way down the

35
00:02:50.972 --> 00:02:54.816
river. It took a lot of paddling to get back to the island.

36
00:02:56.077 --> 00:02:59.200
After we got to shore, we carried everything back to our cave.

37
00:03:03.056 --> 00:03:07.940
After breakfast, I wanted to talk about the dead man and how he came to be killed, but

38
00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:09.121
Jim didn't want to.

39
00:03:09.982 --> 00:03:14.465
He said it would bring bad luck, and the dead man might even come back and haunt us.

40
00:03:15.786 --> 00:03:20.250
But I couldn't help thinking about him, wondering who he was and why he was murdered.

41
00:03:21.771 --> 00:03:26.555
We looked at the clothes we had taken and found eight dollars in coins sewed into the lining

42
00:03:26.575 --> 00:03:27.055
of the coat.

43
00:03:28.904 --> 00:03:33.245
I told Jim that he was wrong to say we'd have bad luck because now we were having

44
00:03:33.305 --> 00:03:33.705
good luck.

45
00:03:35.166 --> 00:03:37.927
But Jim just said that the bad luck was still coming.

46
00:03:39.247 --> 00:03:40.247
And he was sure right.

47
00:03:42.928 --> 00:03:46.589
A few days later, I went into the cave while Jim was outside.

48
00:03:47.569 --> 00:03:49.790
I found a rattlesnake in there and killed it.

49
00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:54.991
I thought it would be funny to leave the snake curled up on Jim's bed as if it

50
00:03:55.031 --> 00:03:55.791
were still alive.

51
00:03:56.712 --> 00:04:00.185
When bedtime came, Jim climbed into bed and gave a yell.

52
00:04:02.006 --> 00:04:06.249
The dead snake's mate had crawled in beside it and had bitten Jim on the foot!

53
00:04:07.089 --> 00:04:08.270
I killed it with a stick.

54
00:04:10.051 --> 00:04:13.973
Jim believed in old-fashioned ways to save yourself from a snake's poison.

55
00:04:15.334 --> 00:04:19.036
He said I had to roast the snake and give him a piece of it to eat.

56
00:04:20.336 --> 00:04:24.899
He also told me to make a bracelet from the snake's rattles and tie it around his wrist.

57
00:04:26.239 --> 00:04:26.840
I did that too.

58
00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:31.982
I also brought him the whiskey jug to drink from because he was thirsty.

59
00:04:33.563 --> 00:04:37.285
Jim's foot and leg swelled up and stayed that way for four days.

60
00:04:38.726 --> 00:04:42.148
On the fifth day, he began to feel better and the swelling went down.

61
00:04:43.969 --> 00:04:51.413
But Jim warned me, "Handling a snakeskin brings so much bad luck that we probably haven't come to

62
00:04:51.433 --> 00:04:52.513
the end of it yet."

63
00:04:53.894 --> 00:04:57.556
The days passed by and the river went down to its normal level again.

64
00:04:58.876 --> 00:05:01.278
I was beginning to get tired of staying on the island.

65
00:05:02.379 --> 00:05:05.081
I wanted to go back to our town and see what was going on.

66
00:05:06.362 --> 00:05:09.445
Jim told me that I should go at night and be very careful.

67
00:05:11.006 --> 00:05:13.628
Then he got the idea that I should dress up as a girl.

68
00:05:14.749 --> 00:05:18.652
I put on a dress and a sunbonnet that we had taken from the floating house.

69
00:05:19.853 --> 00:05:22.055
Then he made me practice walking like a girl.

70
00:05:23.376 --> 00:05:27.340
He said I had to stop lifting up my dress to get things out of my pants pocket.

71
00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:32.423
I paddled over to town in the canoe and tied it up.

72
00:05:33.724 --> 00:05:36.628
Nearby a light was shining in a shabby little house.

73
00:05:37.729 --> 00:05:41.333
I peeked in the window and saw a middle-aged woman sitting at a table.

74
00:05:42.374 --> 00:05:46.078
I thought I knew everyone in town, but I'd never seen this woman before.

75
00:05:47.079 --> 00:05:47.940
I knocked on the door.
